{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Root cause confirmed on origin/main 1c8a67702f8. The handler that outlives the test is the entrypoint stderr handler (marker _rebar_stderr_handler) built by install_stderr_handler in src/rebar/_logging.py as StreamHandler(sys.stderr), installed by rebar._cli.main (src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py:316-318). A scratch pytest plugin listing the rebar logger's handlers after each test showed that, after test_cli_passed_but_unsigned_is_exit_11_with_byte_identical_stderr, this handler holds that test's capsys CaptureIO with closed=True and stays attached for the next test. The install is idempotent by marker, so later main() calls never rebind it. Production is at fault: any in-process caller whose sys.stderr is swapped or closed gets dead or misdirected diagnostics. Polluter: the first test on a worker to call rebar._cli.main under capsys; in the reported pair, the plan-review CLI test. A second, test-side order dependence: the plan-review test's byte-identical stderr assertion also captured _seed's output, which logs an unsigned-write warning once any earlier main() has installed the handler; with a lazy-stderr probe it failed in order verify,plan-review. Fix: _CurrentStderrHandler resolves sys.stderr at emit time (the pattern of the stdlib's logging._StderrHandler), and the plan-review test drains seeding output before main(). Evidence: tests/unit/test_logging_stderr_target.py fails 2 of 2 on the old _logging.py (ValueError: I/O operation on closed file) and passes 2 of 2 after. The pair passes in both orders, and both facade modules together pass 29 of 29 in both orders (-p no:randomly -p no:xdist). tests/interfaces plus the logging/CLI/MCP/reconciler modules: 2841 passed, 12 skipped. make lint and make typecheck exit 0."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793815047210806001,"uuid":"c134fca3-1c93-4cfa-be29-95443af26174"}